Z||000000||fierojunky||05-08-2001||01:17 PM||||Well i decided it was time to swap out the factory speakers in my car last weekend and i popped the front speaker covers off - and did the same to the rear - DOH - Now i need the drivers side interior pannel - why aren't the rears covers?  the are accutually part of the panel???  LMK||||reg||9
Z||000001||sqoach||05-08-2001||01:39 PM||||I did that too when I was changing out my speakers. All I did is glue them back on. Also might be able to put some short screws in from the back. And yes, they are part of the panel. You need to take off the two seatbelt bolts and the screw in the door jam.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">   <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||11
Z||000002||TheFiero64||05-09-2001||12:49 PM||||That is why I loved having my parts car. I would try something on that, then if it broke I knew not to do it that way on the other car.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
Z||000003||Fiero5||05-09-2001||12:52 PM||||That's assuming of course that your parts car is the same model style and features as your driver.<BR>Kinda hard to try out the speakers in the back for example if your parts car is an 84 or 85 and vise versa, versa visa.<P>Steve||||reg||12
